e  southeast it looks like he's getting  ready to make that decision so margaret  give us some context here uh part of the  pretext for vladimir putin's  machinations is his claim that he's  repeated over and over again which is  that the united states pledged back in  1990 that they would not expand nato  eastward i think that would mean  including ukraine but that's not really  true he does seem to have a historical  you know he there's something about  ukraine  that he wants explain that to our  viewers well  in terms of moving eastward ukraine as  even president biden said isn't about to  join nato they've been sort of  twisting in the wind since 2008 they  would say and they haven't met the  standard for being admitted so that  hasn't changed in terms of the  provocation that vladimir putin may be  claiming is there but  in terms of how that would matter moving  the borders and this is the nightmare  scenario is getting uh nato troops on  high alert so close in proximity to  russian troops that any errant shot any  you know right turn russian forces could  make could spark a broader conflict but  in terms of the window for negotiation  the united states says these maximalist  positions put them in a really tough  spot because they can't say ukraine you  will never join even though there's no  active process underway to pull them in  to nato so uh that is sort of the  standoff the things that are being  offered are arms control talks other  options we seem to be really focused on  ukraine in a way um obviously you know  the nato forces are seem to be behind  this country but  i'm i'm curious for folks who don't  understand the politics here you know  why wouldn't a better deterrent be  for  vladimir putin to be staring back at a  force  that's that's equally aligned on the  border right well  the us military would say that russia  will have air dominance they will  overwhelm the ukraine forces and  president biden has said he won't send  americans to die for ukr